# Todo and history hygiene

`docs/todo/` is **open work only**. Finished work belongs in `docs/todo/HISTORY.md`.

## While working

- One file per in-progress task: `docs/todo/<short-name>.md` (plan, status, leftovers).
- Session notes in `docs/worklogs/` only while that session still has open follow-ups.
- Do not edit `docs/remaining-work.md`, `docs/features.md`, or
  `docs/todo/HISTORY.md` until the PR is otherwise ready to merge. Stack related
  PRs. See `pr-stacking.mdc`.

## When the PR is ready to merge

1. Append a **compact** dated section to `docs/todo/HISTORY.md` (filename, what shipped, PR if any). Do not dump full transcripts.
2. Move leftover open items into `docs/remaining-work.md` or a new slim todo file.
3. Strip `[x]` / "✅ done" rows from `docs/remaining-work.md`, worklogs, and plan docs. That checklist is open/`[~]` only.
4. Update `docs/features.md` only if the product surface changed.

Do this in **one** commit on the PR that is merging, not on every intermediate
push. After it lands on main, delete the todo file and any matching worklog.

## Before starting new work

Skim `docs/todo/` (not HISTORY). Do not start by rewriting the shared catalogs.
If a todo is already shipped, fold it only in a ready-to-merge commit.

Do not invent a second backlog. Roadmap status stays in `docs/project-roadmap.md`.
